course: dictionary
lesson: 14311
title: Oatmeal: food or colour?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and oatmeal is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Mum stirred the oatmeal into the pan for our breakfast» tells you oatmeal is food, here crushed oats cooked into porridge.
explain: Oatmeal can also be a colour. «I need a new oatmeal jumper for school» is not about food at all. The clue is the word jumper, which you wear. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense with a food, or with a colour?
explain: In the USA and Canada, oatmeal can mean a bowl of hot porridge. «Dad made oatmeal with bananas and honey.» Here it is the cooked dish you eat, not the oats in a packet. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Oatmeal is oats that have been crushed or ground.
fact: Oatmeal is used to make porridge, oatcakes and biscuits.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «oatmeal» can mean hot porridge made from oats.
fact: «Oatmeal» can also be a pale greyish-brown colour, like oats.
fact: Oats give slow energy and fibre, so oatmeal is a good breakfast food.
exercise: «Mum stirred the oatmeal into the pan for our breakfast.» What is oatmeal here? | A type of wool | A kind of biscuit tin | A pale greyish-brown colour | * Crushed oats for food
exercise: «The new carpet in the hall is a soft oatmeal colour.» What does oatmeal describe? | * A pale greyish-brown colour | A sort of bread | A food for breakfast | A type of rain
exercise: «In Canada, Grandma ordered a bowl of oatmeal at the diner.» What does oatmeal mean here? | A pale brown jumper | A type of cake | * Hot porridge made from oats
test: Which meaning fits «I ate oatmeal cookies after school»? | * Crushed oats used in baking | A wet, grey day | A pale greyish-brown colour | A kind of coat
test: Which meaning fits «Her oatmeal scarf matched her coat perfectly»? | A bowl of hot porridge | Crushed oats for baking | * A pale greyish-brown colour | A type of pet food
exam: In «The walls were painted oatmeal», what tells you oatmeal is a colour? | Oatmeal is always food | * The word painted | The word walls | The word were
